  "result": "Done! I've added line discount support to the invoicing system:\n\n**Updated src/invoices.js:**\n- `createInvoice()` now accepts `discountPercent` (0-100, can be decimal)\n  - Validates range and type, returns DISCOUNT_INVALID if invalid\n  - Defaults to 0 if not provided\n- `addLine()` now accepts `discountPercent` parameter with same validation\n  - When merging existing SKUs, uses the new discount value\n- `invoiceTotals()` now computes discounts:\n  - Returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }` instead of just `{ subtotal, total }`\n  - `discount` = sum of line discounts (each rounded with roundCents)\n  - `total` = max(0, subtotal - discount) to enforce clamping rule\n\n**Updated src/errors.js:**\n- Added DISCOUNT_INVALID error code\n\n**Tests:**\n- Updated 3 existing invoiceTotals tests to check the new discount field\n- Added 13 new test cases covering:\n  - Discount validation (range, type, decimals)\n  - Proper discount calculation\n  - Multiple lines with different discounts\n  - Total clamping at 0 (when discount exceeds subtotal)\n  - Line merging with new discount values\n- All 85 tests pass\n\n**Project decision:** No computed amount can ever go below zero\u2014all are clamped at 0.",
